DIAG: ath12k: skip the monitor status ring's HTT setup

Temporary, not for upstream -- this disables the monitor status path.

Bisecting ath12k_dp_rx_htt_setup with six second sleeps found the single
message that takes the Q6 down. The refill buffer ring is survived in
full; this one is followed by the fault 243 ms later, with the RX TLV
filter not yet sent:

  15.847  htt[0] rx_refill_buf
  15.851  htt[3] mon_status_refill
  15.856  sleeping 6s
  16.099  fatal error
  22.237  survived 6s
  22.237  htt[4] rxdma_ring_sel_config

So ath12k_dp_tx_htt_srng_setup(..., HAL_RXDMA_MONITOR_STATUS) is what the
firmware cannot take. Skip it and see whether the rest comes up.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
@@ -4651,18 +4651,15 @@
 			return ret;
 		}
 	} else {
-		for (i = 0; i < ab->hw_params->num_rxdma_per_pdev; i++) {
-			ring_id =
-				dp->rx_mon_status_refill_ring[i].refill_buf_ring.ring_id;
-			ret = ath12k_dp_tx_htt_srng_setup(ab, ring_id, i,
-							  HAL_RXDMA_MONITOR_STATUS);
-			if (ret) {
-				ath12k_warn(ab,
-					    "failed to configure mon_status_refill_ring%d %d\n",
-					    i, ret);
-				return ret;
-			}
-		}
+		/* DIAG: this is the message that kills the Q6.
+		 *
+		 * Bisecting ath12k_dp_rx_htt_setup with sleeps put the fault
+		 * 243 ms after this call and before the next one: the refill
+		 * buffer ring is survived for six seconds, this is not.
+		 *
+		 * Skip it to find out whether everything else comes up.
+		 */
+		pr_warn("ath12k DBG: SKIPPING mon_status_refill htt setup\n");
 	}
 
 	ret = ab->hw_params->hw_ops->rxdma_ring_sel_config(ab);
